{
  "schemaVersion": "tracy-personalize/v1",
  "note": "What tools/personalize.mjs changes on a customer's copy of this template from the questionnaire answers (seed/questions.json). Five kinds, and the difference between them is what may be INVENTED: `identity` is the customer's own words, written exactly; `replace` rewrites the demo brand everywhere; `copy` is prose a model writes for their sector; `rewrite` does the same for whole demo entries; `facts` are CLAIMS about a real business — counts, founding years, certifications, named clients — and those are REMOVED, never written: a made-up \"380 projects since 2004\" is a lie in the customer's name (CLAUDE.md §0 rule 3). `hide` unpublishes pages that are nothing but claims and drops their menu items. Values use {name} {NAME} {initials} {phone} {address} {year} {sector}; a rule whose value needs an answer the customer did not give is skipped and reported, never guessed.",
